        {
          "question": "e-4379",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C-(B+A) & =A+C-B-A \\\\  & =\\cancel{A}+C-B-\\cancel{A} \\\\  & =C-B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C-B & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3-3 & -1-(-1) \\\\ 1-2 & 2-0 \\\\ -6-(-4) & 1-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
